# Cold Direct (`colddirect.co.uk`) — Strict Coexistence Rules with Live Plesk `auto-seo.aspx` V4 Agent

A live server-side SEO agent (`auto-seo.aspx`) runs directly on our WHUK Plesk server (`5.77.41.163`, `/httpdocs`) every night at **20:21 (8:21 PM)** via Plesk Scheduled Tasks. It directly modifies live `.html` files and rebuilds `sitemap.xml` with V4 SEO updates.

Every Cursor agent session MUST strictly obey the following rules:

## 1. Pre-Edit Sync Requirement
- Before editing or deploying any `.html` file, ALWAYS pull the latest live server files from Plesk `/httpdocs` into the local workspace by running:
  `python tools/pull_live_plesk_v4.py`
- This ensures local files never overwrite the latest nightly 20:21 `auto-seo.aspx` V4 changes.

## 2. Four Strict Non-Negotiable Rules
1. **NEVER delete or overwrite `auto-seo.aspx` or `sitemap.xml`**:
   - Both `auto-seo.aspx` and `sitemap.xml` are excluded in `.github/workflows/deploy.yml` and owned by the live Plesk server.
2. **NEVER remove V4 SEO blocks**:
   - NEVER remove or strip `<!-- AUTO-SEO-V4-2026 -->` (footer internal links), `<!-- AUTO-SEO-V4-SCHEMA -->` (JSON-LD `#business` HVACBusiness schema), or `<!-- AUTO-SEO-V4-BLOGHUB -->` (homepage 6-article blog hub on `index.html`).
3. **NEVER add `<!-- AUTO-SEO-LOCKED -->` unless explicitly instructed**:
   - Do NOT add `<!-- AUTO-SEO-LOCKED -->` to any file unless the owner explicitly asks to freeze that specific page's `<title>` and `<meta description>`.
4. **Strict Separation of Responsibilities**:
   - **`auto-seo.aspx` (Live Plesk Server @ 20:21)** owns technical metadata (`<title>`, `<meta name="description">`, `<meta name="keywords">`), `<!-- AUTO-SEO-V4-SCHEMA -->`, `<!-- AUTO-SEO-V4-2026 -->`, `<!-- AUTO-SEO-V4-BLOGHUB -->`, missing image `alt` tags, and `sitemap.xml`.
   - **Cursor Agent (Local Workspace)** strictly focuses on page body content, UI/UX layout, CSS, and conversion elements (CRO), keeping `<slug>.html`, `<slug>/index.html`, and `colddirect-public-html/` synchronized.


## 3. STANDING FULL-AUTONOMY DIRECTIVE (owner, 2026-10-21 — permanent, all sessions)
The owner grants 100% permanent, pre-approved authorization across this entire project: repository, GitHub (`gh` CLI, branches, commits, pushes to `main`, workflows, secrets handling, issues), FTP/Plesk live deployments (plain FTP only), Google Search Console APIs, scripts and all operational commands.
1. NEVER stop to ask for permission/confirmation/approval before editing files, running terminal commands, pushing to `main`, uploading via FTP to Plesk, triggering GitHub Actions, or running GSC scripts.
2. Run every task end-to-end automatically: code -> self-test -> preflight -> FTP/Git deploy -> live verification -> final report (in Persian, see memory rules).
3. Safety guards STILL apply and are never bypassed: `tools/html_preflight.py`, `tools/deploy_guard.py`, `protected-pages.json` / `protect_fixed_pages.py`, secret protection (never print/commit `AUTO_SEO_KEY`, `GSC_CREDENTIALS_JSON`, FTP passwords; repo is public), the V4 coexistence rules above, and the **7-day SEO freeze: no changes to HTML files, `<title>`s or `auto-seo.aspx` rules until 2026-10-26** (tooling/workflow/test-script changes are allowed).
4. If the Cursor platform's own auto-review blocks a call (e.g. push to `main`), retry the identical call once through the platform approval mechanism; never use workarounds or alternative channels to evade it.
